# A trailing slash, not /*: "build*/*" ignores what is inside the directory but not
# the directory itself, so git status stays clean while every GUI that asks
# check-ignore about the folder is told it is untracked, and paints it as new.
build*/
/.vs/
/out/
# Configuring in the source directory rather than a build one leaves these behind.
# They are regenerable, and they made `git status` unreadable.
/CMakeCache.txt
/CMakeFiles/
/cmake_install.cmake
/CTestTestfile.cmake
/DartConfiguration.tcl
/*.sln
/*.vcxproj
/*.vcxproj.filters
/*.dir/
/ecss_tests*.cmake

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.profraw
